//? Title: Implicit trapezoidal integration: actual Newton residuals and accepted steps
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
The trapezoidal rule is second order and A-stable for solved linear test
equations, but each nonlinear implicit step still needs a successful numerical
solve. Actual predictor, derivative and residual histories retain the original
decay and stiff-decay experiments.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

At each grid interval h solve g(Y)=Y-y-h/2*(f(t,y)+f(t+h,Y))=0. Start with the
forward-Euler predictor, approximate g derivative from an actual representable
forward perturbation, and apply Newton corrections. Accept only when the
recomputed g residual meets atol+rtol*max(abs(y),abs(Y)); a tiny correction
alone does not certify the equation. The linear test equation has amplification
G(z)=(1+z/2)/(1-z/2), which is A-stable but tends to-1 for strongly negative z,
so the method is not L-stable and stiff oscillations can decay slowly. These
mathematical properties assume the implicit steps are solved; finite Newton
convergence is explicitly reported.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/trapezoidal_ode_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/trapezoidal_ode.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::trapezoidal_ode_trace([](double, double y) {
        return -y;
    }, 1, 0, .1, 1);
    std::print("| actual correction attempt | guess | implicit residual | sampled argument | numerical " "derivative | correction assigned | next | residual after |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | " "---: | --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.newton)
        std::print("| {} | {:.12g} | {:.9g} | {:.12g} | {:.12g} | {} | {:.12g} | {:.9g} |\n",
                   s.iteration, s.guess, s.residual, s.perturbation,
                   s.derivative, s.corrected, s.next, s.residual_after);
    std::print("Actual accepted step {}; stop {}.\n", r.converged, r.stop);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual yprime=-y, y0=1, h.1");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual Newton assignments",
                                     r.newton_updates));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("{} actually accepted steps",
                                     r.completed_steps));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/trapezoidal_ode_tiny.svg");
}
```
