> API and interpretation

Finite inputs, nonempty callback and strictly positive steps are required;
backward time is allowed. Last grid time is pinned exactly to t1, and zero
elapsed span copies states without invoking the RHS. Run output retains only
converged accepted trajectory points plus honest failed-step diagnostics; the
compatibility wrapper throws on unresolved Newton work. Callback side
effects/exceptions cannot be rolled back, and RHS evaluation counts reflect the
actual checked implementation rather than the old repeated callback order.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

